
====================================================================================================
K0-K2  TASK 1 -- f(x,v,t) -> stress tensor; the tether is the displacement constraint
====================================================================================================
  The medium: N elements of mass m, distribution f(x,v,t), n = int f d3v, rho = m n,
  ubar_i = <v_i>, delta v_i = v_i - ubar_i, Sigma_ij = <delta v_i delta v_j>.

  K0  the three bands reproduce A29 from the npz (provenance)
      INNER u = 0.3348 +- 0.0563   <w> = -0.2217
      MID   u = 0.4716 +- 0.0361   <w> = -0.1761
      OUTER u = 0.9865 +- 0.0984   <w> = -0.0045
K0 PASS 0.3348/0.4716/0.9865 A29 values +-1e-3 :: the npz and the estimator reproduce A29's three-band inversion; <w> = (u-1)/3
K1 PASS residuals 0, 0 == 0 exactly :: int v_i v_j f d3v = n(ubar_i ubar_j + Sigma_ij): the stress of a kinetic medium is the second moment, T^ij = rho ubar^i ubar^j + rho Sigma^ij.  No other term can appear
K2 PASS O(xi) coefficient 0; O(xi^2) rhobar*Derivative(xi(q), q)**2 0 / rhobar*xi'^2 :: mass conservation rho d3x = rhobar d3q gives rho - rhobar = -rhobar div(xi) + O(xi^2); with P = -rhobar xi this is EXACTLY the theory's div P = rho - rhobar.  The polarization is the mass displacement, not an analogy
K3 PASS p/(rho sigma^2) = 1 == 1 :: isotropic dispersion: p_kin = rho sigma^2 and w_kin = p/(rho c^2) = sigma^2/c^2 >= 0
      n=2: xi*phi' - n*phi = 0   (3p_T = n eps_T)
      n=3: xi*phi' - n*phi = 0   (3p_T = n eps_T)
      n=4: xi*phi' - n*phi = 0   (3p_T = n eps_T)
      Monte-Carlo n=2: <xi phi'>= 2.000000 (exact 2); p_T/eps_T = 0.666667 (exact 0.666667)
      Monte-Carlo n=3: <xi phi'>= 3.000000 (exact 3); p_T/eps_T = 1.000000 (exact 1.000000)
      Monte-Carlo n=4: <xi phi'>= 4.000000 (exact 4); p_T/eps_T = 1.333333 (exact 1.333333)
K4 PASS 3p_T/eps_T = 0.6667/1.0000/1.3333 n/3 = 0.6667/1/1.3333 :: the virial identity 3 p_T = <rho xi.grad phi_T> = n eps_T for a power-law tether: harmonic n=2 gives p_T = (2/3) eps_T.  The tether pressure TRACKS the sign of the tether energy

  THE RESULT OF TASK 1:
      T^00 = rho c^2 + rho sigma^2/2 + eps_T ,  T^ij = rho ubar^i ubar^j + rho Sigma^ij
             + p_T delta^ij ,   p_T = (n/3) eps_T
      w = p/(rho c^2) = [ rho sigma^2 + (n/3) eps_T ] / (rho c^2)          (A43.1)
      u = 1 + 3w = 1 + 3 sigma^2/c^2 + n eps_T/(rho c^2)                   (A43.2)

  For the measured u, the tether must supply n eps_T/(rho c^2) = u - 1:
      INNER  u = 0.3348 -> eps_T/(rho c^2) = -0.3326  (n=2)
      MID    u = 0.4716 -> eps_T/(rho c^2) = -0.2642  (n=2)
      OUTER  u = 0.9865 -> eps_T/(rho c^2) = -0.0068  (n=2)

====================================================================================================
K6-K9  TASK 1/2(i) -- the sign theorem, the virial theorem, and the dispersion route
====================================================================================================
K6 FAIL min w over (sigma, eps_T/rho c^2 in [0,0.5]) = -3.333e-01 >= 0 :: a stable (positive-definite) tether has eps_T >= 0, hence p_T >= 0, hence w >= 0: eq (A43.5) can violate the null energy condition only through eps_T < 0

  K7  force balance for a medium whose displacement is the polarization:
      0 = -(1/rho) d(rho sigma^2)/dr + g + f_T  =>  p_T = rho(sigma^2 + Phi) + const
      p_tot = rho sigma^2 + p_T = rho(2 sigma^2 + Phi)
      w(r) = [2 sigma^2(r) + Phi(r)] / c^2                                  (A43.7)
      isothermal sphere: sigma^2 = GM/(2r) = -Phi/2  =>  w = 0 EXACTLY
K7 PASS 2 sigma^2 + Phi = 0 == 0 (sympy) :: the virialized isothermal sphere constrained to the polarization has w = 0 EXACTLY (sigma^2 = GM/2r = -Phi/2), and a cold free-falling one has w = sigma^2/c^2 ~ 0: either way u = 1 to 1e-5, a second route to A29's u_OUT = 0.9865 +- 0.0984. The same formula bounds the mechanism: w lies in [Phi/c^2, 0], 4.4 decades all below the measurement
      at r = 0.6 Mpc: Phi/c^2 = -7.496e-06  =>  w in [-7.496e-06, 0]
      measured <w>_MID = -0.1761: shortfall 2.350e+04x
K7b PASS |w_meas|/(|Phi|/c^2) = 2.350e+04 > 1e4 :: the tether mechanism spans [Phi/c^2, 0] = 4.4 decades, ALL of them below the measurement by 2.3e4: the sign is right, the amplitude is the gravitational-potential-to-rest-energy ratio
      w = -1/6 at sigma = 0 needs Phi = -c^2/3 (a relativistic potential): this cluster has Phi/c^2 = -7.50e-06, short by 4.45e+04x
      and at virial the same formula gives w = 0 exactly, i.e. u = 1 inside r_sp: the INNER measurement u = 0.335 is 11.8 sigma away
K7c PASS |Phi_need|/|Phi_cluster| = 4.447e+04; virial w=0 vs w_INNER = 11.8 sigma > 1e4; > 8 sigma :: the tether route reaches w = -1/6 only where |Phi| >= c^2/3, i.e. near a horizon; worse, (A43.3) is negative only for a SUB-virial medium (sigma^2 < -Phi/2), so it predicts w < 0 where the medium is young/unrelaxed -- and the inner band is the OLDEST, most relaxed material. The tether inherits A29's sign no-go (11.8 sigma) as well as the amplitude shortfall
K8 PASS min w over beta in [-10,1] = 0.000e+00 >= 0 :: w = (sigma_r^2 + 2 sigma_t^2)/(3c^2): the trace depends only on the SUM of the dispersions, so anisotropy redistributes pressure without ever changing its sign. Rotation enters as bulk motion rho u^i u^j and can only ADD to the trace. No anisotropy is 'needed': none works
K9 PASS sigma_need = c/sqrt6 = 1.2239e+08 m/s = 0.4082 c = 1.469e+04 sigma_c; w(sigma_c) = 7.721e-10 ratio > 1e4; shortfall > 1e8 :: route (i): w = sigma^2/c^2, so w = -1/6 needs sigma^2 = -c^2/6 -- impossible for a positive dispersion; even the |w| = 1/6 MAGNITUDE needs sigma = 0.408c, 1.47e4x the cold medium's own 8.33 km/s. The cold sector is non-relativistic by construction (THEORY s3.3), so its kinetic pressure is 7.7e-10 rho c^2: 2.2e8 short

