K13 PASS mu(1)=1/2 exact; r(X=1) = 0.0200 Mpc vs measured u=1/2 at 1.0652 Mpc (factor 53.26) identical at X=1; factor > 3 :: route (iii): at half capacity u = mu and u = 1-mu coincide exactly at 1/2, so 0.47 does not select either; and half capacity sits at g = a0, r = 0.20 Mpc -- 5.3x inside the measured crossing at 1.07 Mpc. Neither reading gives 0.47 at the radius where the data have it
K14 PASS chi2/dof: mu 40.11, 1-mu 57.51, const 5.92, step 1.45 mu and 1-mu > 10; Delta chi2 vs step > 100 :: both saturation readings are monotone over 1.5 decades in radius; the data are a PLATEAU at 0.33-0.53 out to 1.18 Mpc and then a step to 1. They are rejected at Delta chi2 = 312 / 451 against the step, for zero extra parameters. The step recomputes A29's 1.455 (dof 6); the constant recomputes 5.920 (dof 7)
K15 PASS data u-step at X = 0.0215 (g = 2.013e-12 m/s^2); half capacity at X = 1: factor 46.49 factor > 4 :: the measured u-transition sits at g ~ 0.13 a0, not at the law's half-capacity point g = a0. So route (iii) does not merely mis-normalise: it puts the transition 7x too far out in acceleration. 0.47 is 'near' 1/2 only because the measured plateau value happens to be there; the transition itself is elsewhere

